---
description: Project-wide conventions and workflow for Mailpulse
alwaysApply: true
---

# Ruff after edits

After making code changes in this repository, unless the user explicitly says not to, run:

`uv run ruff check --fix mailpulse && uv run ruff format mailpulse`

# Tests for new functionality

When you add new functionality (routes, services, core behavior, or other user-facing or contract-changing behavior), add or extend automated tests in the same change so the new behavior is covered, unless the user explicitly says not to.

# README updates

After making changes, update `README.md` in the same change when needed so it stays accurate. That includes new or changed setup steps, configuration or environment variables, API surface, CLI usage, or anything else a reader would reasonably expect to find there. Skip README edits when the change does not affect what the README documents, unless the user asks otherwise.

# Control flow

Avoid one-line if/else forms (including ternary expressions). Use a normal `if` / `else` block so branches stay easy to read and step through.

```python
# bad — ternary crammed on one line
timeout = short_timeout if fast_path else long_timeout

# good — explicit branches
if fast_path:
    timeout = short_timeout
else:
    timeout = long_timeout
```

